# Kubernetes addons (portable)

When the ask is MetalLB, ingress-nginx, CloudNativePG (CNPG), or Redis on
Kubernetes, stay inside `kubernetes` craft. Do **not** invent a dedicated
marketplace plugin for each addon.

## MetalLB

- Prefer the project’s existing IPAddressPool / L2Advertisement (or BGP)
  pattern — never invent pool CIDRs.
- List/resolve pool and service LoadBalancer IPs before changing them.
- Changing advertised ranges that carry live ingress needs an explicit verb
  (`kubernetes-safety`).

## ingress-nginx

- Prefer the cluster’s existing IngressClass and controller values.
- Pair TLS/DNS with `traefik` / `nginx-proxy-manager` / `cloudflare` only when
  those surfaces own the edge — do not mix controllers in one change.
- Do not widen default backend or expose admin without an explicit ask.

## CloudNativePG / Postgres operators

- Prefer the project’s existing Cluster / ScheduledBackup CRDs.
- Never invent storage classes, backup destinations, or superuser passwords
  into manifests — credentials stay in Vault/ESO (`kubernetes-external-secrets`).
- Destructive: drop cluster, change primary, or wipe PVCs need an explicit
  verb naming the object.

## Redis

- Prefer the project’s existing Deployment/StatefulSet/Helm values for Redis.
- Do not commit Redis passwords; use ExternalSecret / Vault wiring.
- Flush/all-keys wipe and PVC delete need an explicit verb.

## Defaults

1. Match packaging already in the repo (Helm chart, raw manifests, Kustomize).
2. Never invent cluster-specific CIDRs, storage classes, or ingress IPs.
3. Site topology stays in private overlays — keep this rule agnostic.
